WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.630
It's Wednesday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.480
Room to learn. On 8GB PCs, Windows 11 is now up to 20% more responsive.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.690
Multitasking's up to 40% faster in Microsoft's lab, and open tabs reload less.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.630
In Ontario,

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:38.490
the Hamilton-Wentworth board set November 3 to switch on Copilot for grades 9 to 12.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.720
Students get Study and Learn only. The board's rule?

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.010
Technology supports learning; it doesn't drive it.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.980
Meanwhile, teachers are generating their own city in Minecraft with Arnis,

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.280
an open-source tool.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.550
Every student improves the same park,

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:59.580
then the class compares. Nearly 900,000 downloads so far.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.540
Teachers,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.680
in January OneDrive's due to let you approve a whole class's access requests at once.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.890
Due in December, Teams admins can choose which risky file types to block,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.460
or keep Microsoft's list.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.190
For university IT,

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:21.730
Azure Migrate can now discover and assess NetApp and Dell file storage, in preview.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.100
For student coders,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.340
.NET Conf is free online from November 10, launching .NET 11.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.160
Got a student startup? Imagine Cup is opening up to more startups,

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.550
but students keep their own category.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.770
The top student startup wins $25,000 plus

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.050
credits; applications close February 28.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.150
The fine print? Fake free games,

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:52.140
Roblox cheat tools and cracked apps are quietly hijacking PCs for profit.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.110
Meanwhile,

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:58.210
Edge now automatically switches off notifications from sites caught pushing scams.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.620
After hours? The Elder Scrolls VI finally has a name: Sentinel.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.200
No release date yet.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.670
Game Pass gets Football Manager 27 on PC now,

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.530
and Warhammer Survivors on November 10.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.130
Then Thronefall on the 11th: build a kingdom by day, defend it by night.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.580
Snappier 8GB laptops, an AI tutor for teens,

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.220
a stage for student founders: that's room to learn.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
